<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency Check suppressions.

  RULES FOR THIS FILE — read before adding an entry:

  1. A suppression is a statement that a REPORTED vulnerability does not apply
     to this project. It is not a way to make a red build green. If the CVE
     applies, upgrade the dependency instead.

  2. Every entry MUST carry:
       - the CVE id,
       - a <notes> explaining WHY it does not apply here (which code path is
         absent, which feature is not enabled),
       - an expiry date in the notes, no more than 90 days out.

  3. An undated suppression is a permanently disabled gate. Re-review on expiry;
     if the CVE still has no fix, re-date it deliberately rather than leaving it
     open forever.

  4. NEVER raise failBuildOnCVSS in pom.xml to clear a finding. That disables
     the gate for every dependency, forever, invisibly. This file at least makes
     each exemption reviewable in a diff.

  Remediation is always attempted by UPGRADING first: the Tomcat CVEs reported
  against 10.1.42 were fixed by raising spring-boot-starter-parent to 3.5.16 and
  setting a tomcat.version floor of 10.1.55 — NOT by suppression. The two
  entries below are cases where the scanner's version range or affected
  component genuinely does not match this project.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

  <!--
    CVE-2026-40974 — Spring Boot Cassandra auto-configuration does not perform
    hostname verification on the SSL connection to Cassandra.

    NOT APPLICABLE, two independent reasons:
      1. The advisory's own affected-version list is "Spring Boot 4.0.0". This
         project builds on the 3.5.x line, so the range does not match; the
         finding comes from CPE matching on the artifact name, not the version.
      2. There is no Cassandra dependency and no Cassandra auto-configuration in
         this project. The only datastore is PostgreSQL via spring-boot-starter-
         data-jpa, and the driver is org.postgresql:postgresql.

    Re-review by: 2026-11-27 (90 days). If the project ever adds Cassandra, this
    entry MUST be removed and the finding re-assessed.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      Cassandra auto-configuration is not present in this project (PostgreSQL/JPA
      only) and the advisory targets Spring Boot 4.0.0 while this build is on
      3.5.x. Re-review by 2026-11-27.
    ]]></notes>
    <cve>CVE-2026-40974</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    CVE-2026-41855 — deserialization of untrusted data in
    org.springframework.jms.support.converter.MappingJackson2MessageConverter
    (and the Jackson-based JMS converters) in an untrusted JMS environment.

    NOT APPLICABLE: this project has no JMS. There is no jakarta.jms dependency,
    no spring-jms on the classpath, no message listener, no broker connection and
    no MappingJackson2MessageConverter bean. The vulnerable class is not present
    and cannot be reached. The finding is reported against spring-core and
    spring-web because the CPE match is at the "spring framework" product level
    rather than the affected module.

    Re-review by: 2026-11-27 (90 days). If messaging is ever introduced, remove
    this entry first and re-assess before wiring a broker.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      No JMS in this project: no spring-jms/jakarta.jms dependency, no message
      converters or listeners, no broker. The vulnerable class is absent from the
      classpath. Re-review by 2026-11-27.
    ]]></notes>
    <cve>CVE-2026-41855</cve>
  </suppress>

</suppressions>
